From: well0nez <well0nez@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] board: defconfig: enable the gpio keyboard driver

The bench defconfig has CONFIG_KEYBOARD_ADC=m and CONFIG_KEYBOARD_SUN4I_LRADC=y
but leaves CONFIG_KEYBOARD_GPIO unset (verified in the built tree's .config:
`# CONFIG_KEYBOARD_GPIO is not set`), so the `gpio-keys` node added by
0139 would never bind. Built in, not as a module, because the power key has
to work before any userspace has run.

Note this file is not part of the kernel `series`; the build copies it into
arch/arm64/configs/. The paths below are therefore relative to the project
root (/opt/Projekte/h713), apply with `patch -p1` from there.
---
diff -Nur a/mainline/patches/kernel/board/hy200_qz713df_a1_defconfig b/mainline/patches/kernel/board/hy200_qz713df_a1_defconfig
--- a/mainline/patches/kernel/board/hy200_qz713df_a1_defconfig
+++ b/mainline/patches/kernel/board/hy200_qz713df_a1_defconfig
@@ -73,6 +73,7 @@
 CONFIG_RTL8XXXU_UNTESTED=y
 CONFIG_INPUT_EVDEV=y
 CONFIG_KEYBOARD_ADC=m
+CONFIG_KEYBOARD_GPIO=y
 CONFIG_KEYBOARD_SUN4I_LRADC=y
 # CONFIG_INPUT_MOUSE is not set
 CONFIG_INPUT_TOUCHSCREEN=y
